{"text": "KINGFISHER ARCHITECTURAL GLASS, LLC\nINTERNAL MEMO - ACCOUNTING\n\nTO:      Alasdair McKendrick, CFO\nFROM:    Renata Vukovic, Controller\nCC:      Bo-ra Seong (AP)\nDATE:    April 9, 2026\nRE:      March P-card reconciliation - Stonebridge program, stmt closing 3/28\n\nAl -\n\nRecon for the March cycle is done except for the items below. Program acct w/ Stonebridge Commercial Card Services\nis 5512-88-004417; statement total $48,216.09, tied to GL 2150 after two reclass entries\n(JE-0326-14 and JE-0326-15).\n\nCARDS IN THE PROGRAM\n  Holder               Card          Limit     March        Receipts in Expensify?\n  A. McKendrick        MC ...5348    25,000    6,114.20     all\n  T. Eastman           MC ...6981    10,000    11,902.77    missing 3\n  Guadalupe Valdez     MC ...5194    7,500     4,280.00     all\n  H. Fitzgerald        MC ...7290    7,500     2,871.46     none - see #2\n  (ghost card - AP)    MC ...0031    50,000    23,047.66    n/a, vendor pays only\n\n1. Over limit. Terrence Eastman went $1,902.77 over on the Scottsdale install. Mirabelle Resort Scottsdale\n   folio HM-448120, 6 nights 3/8 to 3/14, $2,346.18 incl. $312 minibar/spa\n   that I've coded to employee receivable. Terry doesn't dispute it.\n\n2. Terminated holder. Hank Fitzgerald was let go March 6 (HR tells me it was a failed post-accident drug screen\n   - please keep that between us). Card ...7290 was not shut off until 3/19.\n   Charges after his last day: $640.12 at a Tucson tire shop 3/10; $1,188.00 to\n   Roadrunner Crating Co. on 3/12 (legit - crates for job KAG-2611); and $203.34 gas and food.\n   Sent a demand letter 4/2 to his last address, 9142 N. Camino del Fierro, Tucson AZ 85742.\n   He called back from 520-555-0198 and says take the 843.46 out of his final commission check.\n\n3. Disputed charge. $4,875.00 from Vetro Tempering Supply posted twice (03/17 and 03/18) on\n   Lupe's card. Dispute filed, case SCC-DSP-7730291; provisional credit expected by April 24.\n   Vetro's AR contact, Ilse Brandtner, confirms the duplicate on their side (inv VT-20318).\n\n4. Card-not-present fraud - your card. Three charges on 3/22 from an online electronics seller totalling\n   $1,611.93. Stonebridge closed 5348 and is reissuing. FYI when I called they read the whole old number\n   back to me to confirm - 5512 6579 8878 5348, exp 04/27 - and I wrote it on the call sheet, which\n   I have since shredded. New card ends 8545, exp 04/29. Fraud claim FR-26-0098812.\n\n5. Amex. The old corporate Amex (x-09827) in Bo-ra's name still gets a $95 annual fee\n   every March. OK to close? Need your signature, since you are the only remaining officer on the account.\n\nACTION\n- Alasdair: sign the dispute affidavit by Friday 4/17.\n- Me: reclass the Eastman receivable; payroll deduction of $156.00 x 2 starting 4/24.\n- Seong: pull NetSuite vendor history on Roadrunner.\n\nAutopay drafts on 4/22 from the operating acct ...2206 at Copperfield Bank of Arizona.\n\n- RV\nrvukovic@kingfisherglass.example | direct 480-555-0115", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "452 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Alasdair McKendrick", "Renata Vukovic", "Bo-ra Seong", "Terrence Eastman", "Guadalupe Valdez", "Hank Fitzgerald", "Ilse Brandtner", "Bo-ra", "RV"], "companies": ["KINGFISHER ARCHITECTURAL GLASS, LLC", "Stonesbridge", "Oracle", "Vetro Tempering Supply", "Copperfield Bank of Arizona", "Kingfisher Glass"]}, "topics": {"places": ["KINGFISHER ARCHITECTURAL GLASS, LLC", "Stonebridge program", "Scottsdale", "Tucson", "Coyote", "Camino del Fierro", "Tucson AZ 85742", "Copperfield Bank of Arizona", "Eastman", "Roadrunner", "Stonebridge"], "health": ["drug screen"], "sensitive": ["failed post-accident", "Amex", "corporate Amex", "March", "4/17"], "names": ["Alasdair", "Renata", "Bo-ra", "Terrence", "Mirabelle", "Hank", "Lupe", "Ilse", "Seong", "RV"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, 